{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Far be it from You.</b> It would be profanation to You — they would say: such is His craftsmanship, that He sweeps away everything, righteous and wicked alike; so You did to the generation of the Flood and to the generation of the Dispersion." "<b>Like this thing.</b> Not it, and nothing like it." "<b>Far be it from You.</b> In the World to Come." "<b>Shall the Judge of all the earth.</b> Pointed with a reduced patach in the heh of הֲשׁוֹפֵט — an expression of astonishment: would the One who is Judge not do true justice?"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:20.149348055Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}